<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 21 April, from 753 BCE to 1960.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/romulus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romulus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">753 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,779 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Romulus founds Rome, according to Roman tradition</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Roman writers placed the city's foundation by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus">Romulus</a> on the Palatine on 21 April 753 BCE, a date fixed by the scholar Varro. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> celebrated it each year as the Parilia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1506 CE <span class="tih-ago">520 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Three days of massacre in Lisbon come to an end</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rioting stirred up by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-order">Dominican friars</a> killed between 1,000 and 4,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-christians">New Christians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> forcibly converted in 1497. King Manuel I punished the city and had two of the friars executed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-christians">New Christians</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1782 CE <span class="tih-ago">244 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rama I founds Bangkok as Siam's new capital</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The city pillar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a> was erected on the east bank of the Chao Phraya, marking the official founding of the new royal capital. It replaced Thonburi across the river.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1836 CE <span class="tih-ago">190 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Texans defeat Santa Anna at San Jacinto</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sam-houston">Sam Houston</a>'s army surprised the Mexican camp and won in about eighteen minutes. Santa Anna was captured the next day and forced to order his troops out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>, securing its independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1918 CE <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Red Baron is shot down and killed near Amiens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Manfred von Richthofen, credited with 80 victories, was killed while pursuing an enemy aircraft over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somme-river">Somme</a>. Whether a Canadian pilot or Australian ground gunners fired the fatal shot is still debated.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1960 CE <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brasília is inaugurated as Brazil's capital</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Built in under four years to plans by Lúcio Costa and Oscar Niemeyer, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brasilia">Brasília</a> replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> as capital. It was meant to draw development into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>'s interior.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li></ol>
